[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Elephant Gambit"]
[Variation "3.exd5 e4 4.Qe2"]
[ECO "C40"]
[Character "gambit,sharp"]
[Risk "high"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "development-lead,open-lines"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 2... d5 { The Elephant Gambit. Black hits e4 at once and is happy to give a pawn for quick development and an open centre. [%cal Gd5e4] }
3. exd5 3... e4 { Kicks the knight away. White has to deal with the attacked knight, so Black gains time while the pawn on d5 hangs for now. [%cal Ge4f3] }
4. Qe2 (4. Nd4 Qxd5 5. Nb5 Qd7)
4... Nf6 { Develops, protects the e4 pawn and attacks the pawn on d5, so Black will win the pawn back. [%cal Gf6d5,Gf6e4] }
5. Nc3 (5. d3 Qxd5 6. Nc3 Bb4 7. Bd2)
5... Be7 { Develops and prepares to castle, getting the king off the e-file before White's queen can pin anything on it. }
6. Nxe4 6... Nxd5 { Takes the pawn back, so material is level again, and puts the knight on a strong central square. } 7. Qd1 7... O-O { Castles. The king is safe and the rook is ready to join the fight on the e-file. }
8. Bc4 8... Nc6 { Develops the last knight and puts pressure on the centre. } 9. h3 9... Na5 { Hits the bishop on c4, so White has to trade or retreat it. } 10. Be2 *
